  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nHigh pressure and a cooler, drier airmass will build into the region\ntoday into Thursday. Highs both days will be in the 70s. The surface\nhigh will shift slowly east through the weekend, leading to a \ngradual warming trend. Highs will return back to near normal \nreadings by Sunday.\n\nNorthwest flow will persist aloft into early next week. The warming\ntemperatures will combine with some embedded mid level energy \ndropping southeast across the Great Lakes to bring the next chance \nfor showers and thunderstorms Monday into Tuesday.",
